    "scope": "A real registered environment.check emits environment-v1 using only current runtime/distribution and optional explicit project metadata. No-project calls never discover a root; malformed model/history is uninspected. Active state blocks without recovery. Target aliases resolve to their registered contract without handler execution; missing required prerequisites remain unknown with code 0 and compatible=null. Optional unavailable quotas remain unknown; an observed RLIMIT_AS is qualified only as a process address-space ceiling. Native access recording and effect traps prove the current tested scope is free from probe writes, subprocesses, network and semantic model validation. R preserves W cases and distinguishes proven pending journals from unclassified operational entries: the latter block with code 5 but keep recovery_required=null. Readonly roots, optional invalid/unavailable native limits, unknown CPU/storage quotas, permission failures, unsafe symlinks, regular configuration aliases and concurrent metadata changes retain their actual failure classes without repair. The public environment schema requires runtime/build identity fields and null values for unknown observations; no project secrets or extra environment fields are accepted. C separates optional resource observation from required prerequisites by an AST-preserving extraction; existing machine results and all W/R behavior oracles remain unchanged."
  },
